---
// KV Cache as the trajectory grows over three turns: each turn's new messages pay cache_creation once, then hit on every later turn; nothing earlier moves (redraw of Fig 2-13).
---

<svg
	class="dg"
	viewBox="0 0 720 860"
	role="img"
	aria-labelledby="d2-kcg-title d2-kcg-desc"
	style="min-width: 630px"
>
	<title id="d2-kcg-title">Evolution of KV Cache as the agent trajectory grows</title>
	<desc id="d2-kcg-desc">
		Three columns, one per completed turn, each listing the same eleven message slots. Turn 1 (first load of the
		PPTX skill): system, tools, user_q1, the starred skill_listing, asst: Skill(pptx), its tool_result and the
		starred skill_content are all NEW, and the last four slots are not yet generated; cache_creation for the turn is
		about 2.5k tokens. Turn 2 (read the PDF file): those seven slots are now HIT, and asst: Read(pdf) and its
		tool_result are NEW; cache_creation is about 0.5k tokens. Turn 3 (write HTML): everything through the Read
		result is HIT, and asst: Write(html) and its tool_result are NEW; cache_creation is about 0.4k tokens. Legend:
		NEW means new tokens added this turn, which pay cache_creation once; HIT means already in the cache prefix, a
		free hit this turn; a dash means content not yet generated this turn. The starred attachments are marked
		emit-once: they pay cache_creation only on Turn 1, then are a permanent HIT for all subsequent turns, with
		marginal cost zero. Once inserted, the index position of each message never moves; new content is only appended
		to the end of the array.
	</desc>

	<text x="2" y="28" class="dg-title">KV Cache as the trajectory grows</text>

